WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.386
A document store can keep a nested profile as one
aggregate, with a configured shard key controlling

00:00:06.386 --> 00:00:12.260
distribution A search engine serves another need:
locating documents by terms and relevance.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.433
Find the document-ID list for each normalized term
and return their intersection.

00:00:17.433 --> 00:00:23.196
An application cache stores values that help
construct responses, such as a leaderboard or

00:00:23.196 --> 00:00:29.279
precomputed summary An HTTP reverse-proxy cache
stores reusable responses at a different layer.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:29.471
No.

00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:35.682
If it is designed as a rebuildable cache, the source
records remain elsewhere and the leaderboard

00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:36.835
can be recomputed.

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:43.307
A mounted network filesystem provides a file
interface that existing applications can use Block

00:00:43.307 --> 00:00:49.848
storage instead exposes volumes on which a
filesystem may be built; object storage exposes
named

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:51.824
objects through service APIs.

00:00:51.824 --> 00:00:52.914
Not necessarily.

00:00:52.914 --> 00:00:59.454
It must check required file operations and semantics
against the object API and adapt its access

00:00:59.454 --> 00:00:59.999
pattern.
